Z||000000||84fierotoronto||11-21-2000||10:37 PM||||To be more specific :<BR>It is 84 Fiero 4spd.<BR>When I start the car (in neutral), everything works.  If I put it in first the car tries to move forward and than the engine stalls.  All the time I have my foot pressed on the clutch and when I try to put it in first (with some force) it makes a noize.  When it goes in... the car moves forward a bit and than stalls.  Same goes for reverse.  The car had the clutch and release bearing changed not long ago.  Also I didnt drive it much because I wanted to store it over the winter.  Problems came 2 weeks ago when I couldn't switch from reverse (after backing up) to first.  I had to switch the car off, and than put it in first and than start the car.  It was also very hard to put it from first to second after that. Now and before when the engine is off I can switch in any gear easy.  But when it is running ....  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>I hope you guys can help to let me know whats wrong.  If its something major I'll wait till spring.. if something small I'll do it now.<P>Julian||||reg||9
Z||000001||Phil||11-21-2000||10:56 PM||||Definately  in the clutch system somewhere. Start by checking for air in the system then see if you still have the aluminium clutch pedal(which will be bent) or any "slop" in the linkage. Read V8 Archies stuff on clutch probs. That should give you a place to start||||reg||1
